meta {
  name: What is in session in November
  type: http
  seq: 42
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetable-calendar?branch_id={{branchId}}&from=2026-11-01&to=2026-11-30
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.count: eq 4
  res.body.session_dates: isArray
  res.body.calendar_days: isArray
}

docs {
  calendar_days is every row in the window; session_dates is only the dates
  open for the half asked about. Both are returned because the difference is
  the useful part - four days exist in November, three of them teach.

  branch_id, from and to are all required. Omitting the window is 400 rather
  than defaulting to the year, because the resolver walks days and an
  unbounded walk is a slow way to hang a dashboard.
}
